  "term": "granular layer",
  "definition": "The granular layer is a cell layer in brain regions such as the main and accessory olfactory bulbs. In this source, it is described as a site where researchers measured changes in cell proliferation and the formation of new neurons related to sexual behavior and opioid signaling.",
